// A #local declared in an #in or #when block is a name for that block only:
// its formula runs when the block does, and #end ends the name. Two blocks may
// each have their own, and a rule after the block cannot read it -- it would
// see a value from the last cycle the block ran (local_scope_out).
#variable X = 0
#variable Y = 0
#variable Z = 0

#when X < 5
  #local L = X + 1
  X = L
  #in NORMAL
    Y = L * 10
  #end
#end
#when X >= 5
  #local L = X * 2
  Z = L
#end
